{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LjkZAVBuWzbAiApgf3kuzz","type":"tool_result","content":"=== 1. Phase A artifacts ===\n  SYMBOLS.md    96 lines,  3 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n  ERRORS.md     89 lines, 16 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n  CONFIGS.md   115 lines, 21 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n\n=== 2. Symbol parity (C vs Rust .so) ===\n  C exports:    3  [cleanup cleanup_resources print_result ]\n  Rust exports: 3  [cleanup cleanup_resources print_result ]\n  missing from Rust: ''\n\n=== 3. Rows executed (debug) ===\n  rows passing: 39\n\n=== 4. Source integrity ===\n  src/lib.rs      21d7970159cc948a9785cc94bc62c2ec  (original: 21d7970159cc948a9785cc94bc62c2ec)\n  c_src/src/lib.c 2de43f985026edadf650b90c8aadb022  (original: 2de43f985026edadf650b90c8aadb022)\n  c_src mtimes:   2026-08-19 18:23:49 / 2026-08-19 18:23:49\n\n=== 5. Deliverables added ===\n  mutation_check.py\n  verify_all.sh\n  \n  tests/:\n  common\n  phase_b_valid_paths.rs\n  phase_c_error_paths.rs\n  phase_d_symbol_parity.rs\n  \n  tests/common/:\n  mod.rs\n\n=== 6. Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"translated_rust\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"cleanup_lib\"\n# \"lib\" is present only so that the integration tests in tests/ depend on the\n# lib target and cargo therefore REBUILDS the cdylib before running them.\n# With crate-type = [\"cdylib\"] alone, `cargo test` silently runs against a stale\n# libcleanup_lib.so. The tests still load the cdylib exclusively through\n# libloading/dlsym and never link against or call the rlib.\ncrate-type = [\"lib\", \"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5095bf2-f73b-46dc-a5a6-800abd6dde4f","uuid":"e65a7276-cc2e-4fa2-9b38-25e1703bcaff","timestamp":"2026-08-19T18:47:12.972Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== 1. Phase A artifacts ===\n  SYMBOLS.md    96 lines,  3 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n  ERRORS.md     89 lines, 16 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n  CONFIGS.md   115 lines, 21 table rows, 0 unchecked boxes\n\n=== 2. Symbol parity (C vs Rust .so) ===\n  C exports:    3  [cleanup cleanup_resources print_result ]\n  Rust exports: 3  [cleanup cleanup_resources print_result ]\n  missing from Rust: ''\n\n=== 3. Rows executed (debug) ===\n  rows passing: 39\n\n=== 4. Source integrity ===\n  src/lib.rs      21d7970159cc948a9785cc94bc62c2ec  (original: 21d7970159cc948a9785cc94bc62c2ec)\n  c_src/src/lib.c 2de43f985026edadf650b90c8aadb022  (original: 2de43f985026edadf650b90c8aadb022)\n  c_src mtimes:   2026-08-19 18:23:49 / 2026-08-19 18:23:49\n\n=== 5. Deliverables added ===\n  mutation_check.py\n  verify_all.sh\n  \n  tests/:\n  common\n  phase_b_valid_paths.rs\n  phase_c_error_paths.rs\n  phase_d_symbol_parity.rs\n  \n  tests/common/:\n  mod.rs\n\n=== 6. Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"translated_rust\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"cleanup_lib\"\n# \"lib\" is present only so that the integration tests in tests/ depend on the\n# lib target and cargo therefore REBUILDS the cdylib before running them.\n# With crate-type = [\"cdylib\"] alone, `cargo test` silently runs against a stale\n# libcleanup_lib.so. The tests still load the cdylib exclusively through\n# libloading/dlsym and never link against or call the rlib.\ncrate-type = [\"lib\", \"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n[profile.release]\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w5xg7otzbidy5jjvievr4mc4ms7cv6il6nw52ox6bkxebybtadzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and `c_src/` and `src/lib.rs` are byte-identical to their originals.\n\n## Result: the translation is correct — no Rust fixes were needed\n\n`cleanup`, `print_result`, `cleanup_resources` all match the C byte-for-byte, including the two `switch` fall-throughs (`10→+30`, `30→+70`), two's-complement overflow wrapping, and the `TO_STRING(numbers)` quirk that stringizes the *token* (`\"Processed numbers: numbers\"`, not the values).\n\n**Phase A** — `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (16 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (21 rows). Exactly **one** valid build configuration: no `[features]` in Cargo.toml, no `option()` in CMakeLists, no `#ifdef` in the C. A Phase D test re-derives this each run so adding a feature fails loudly instead of silently under-testing.\n\n**Phases B/C** — 39 differential rows, ~55,000 cross-library calls, comparing both return value **and** exact stdout bytes (fd-1 `dup2` capture; both `.so`s share one glibc `stdout`, so buffering matches by construction). Exhaustive where feasible: all 625 switch-path combinations, all 4096 off-by-one combinations, all 2401 signed-extreme combinations, all 128 non-UTF-8 high bytes.\n\n**Phase D** — symbol diff is empty (3/3), all `dlsym`-resolvable, no non-libc undefined symbols. Green under debug, default features, and `--release`.\n\n## Three bugs I found were in my own test harness, and mattered\n\n1. **The suite was passing vacuously.** With `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` alone, nothing in `tests/` depends on the lib target, so **`cargo test` never rebuilt the `.so`** — it loaded a stale artifact. I proved this: **14/14 injected bugs survived.** Fixed by adding `\"lib\"` to `crate-type` (tests still only use `libloading`/`dlsym`, never the rlib), plus an `assert_so_is_fresh` guard so it can't regress silently.\n2. **Two \"divergences\" were libtest's own progress text** leaking into my capture window, since fd 1 is process-global and rows ran on parallel threads. Restructured to one `#[test]` per binary; also made the fd restore panic-safe via a `Drop` guard.\n3. **My leak probe double-freed**, aborting the release run with glibc's `free(): double free detected in tcache`. My logic assumed \"address not recycled ⇒ not freed\", which is false. It now never re-frees and validates its own tcache precondition, reporting `INCONCLUSIVE` under `--release` rather than faking a pass.\n\n## Blind spot that stdout comparison provably cannot see\n\nMutation testing found that inverting `cleanup_resources`' NULL guard **survived the entire suite** — because `free(NULL)` is a legal no-op and a leak prints nothing. Return-value + stdout comparison is genuinely insufficient here. I added rows **E5/E5b/E6** using a tcache address-recycling probe to observe whether `free` actually ran. `mutation_check.py` now reports **16/16 caught, 0 surviving**, including three pure-leak mutations the original suite missed.\n\nTwo caveats worth stating plainly: rows **E1/E2** guard code that is *statically dead* in the C (`strncmp(\"VALID\",\"VALID\")` is always 0; `malloc(50)` doesn't fail), so they are pinned negatively — asserting the branch's output never appears in either implementation — since triggering them would require editing `c_src/`. And the E5/E6 leak probes rely on a glibc heuristic that holds in debug (where mutation testing runs) but not under `--release`, where they self-report as skipped.\n\nRun everything with `./verify_all.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2029,"cache_read_input_tokens":166895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2029,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5095bf2-f73b-46dc-a5a6-800abd6dde4f","uuid":"31de5654-06ca-420c-a3b6-e7c07901d3af","timestamp":"2026-08-19T18:47:33.147Z"}
